> I'm a lvl 12 samurai on dlvl 14, and I just came across a warhorse. I
> could easily kill him, but since there's a leash on this level (I
> haven't bothered picking one up yet), and since I know where to get a
> saddle (with a lot of backtracking), and since I have two ?oTaming,
> should I bother using him as a mount at this point?

Horses are domesticated.  You can tame it with a carrot or apple
or lichen or so on.  No need for taming - Save them for when it
goes ferral from lack of food sometime in the future.

> Are there any advantages to using a mount as a samurai?

Others have pointed out the speed advantage.  I'll add in the
carrying capacity advantage.  On a horse it takes more weight
to get burdened.

One thing that is available to knights that I don't think is an option
for samurai is jousting with a lance.  It doesn't really matter,
though.
Once a samurai gets to a high enough level it becomes an option
to go Expert in bow/arrow.  Gather all arrows in the game and
carry them down to prepare for that time.  Horse bowmen make
formidable warriors.

> Has this ever worked out for anyone?

Folks ascend riding all sorts of critters.  Note that it takes skill
slots so take that cost into account.



